    "description": "Hosiden Corporation develops, manufactures, and sells electronic components in Japan, Asia, Europe, Vietnam, China, and internationally. The company operates through three segments: Mechanical Components, Acoustic Components, and Composite Components and Others. The Mechanical Components segment offers connectors, jacks, switches, etc. The Acoustic Components segment provides microphones, headphones, headsets, speakers, receivers, etc. The Composite Components and Others segment offers composite equipment. It also manufactures and sells information telecommunications equipment, office machines, electronic, electrical appliances, auto parts, and medical equipment and related parts. In addition, it provides earphones; remote control units; wireless components including modules, bluetooth speaker and low energy beacons, IR headphones, MEDiTAG, and radio devices; and other products, such as chargers, AC adapters, wireless chargers, circuit protectors, and A2B compatible acceleration sensors, as well as display related and sensor products. The company offers its products through dealers. Hosiden Corporation was founded in 1947 and is headquartered in Yao, Japan."
